{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire","id":1265523,"title":"What if Mage has as many books as Vampire?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-08T09:50:02-08:00","id":1265523,"title":"What if Mage has as many books as Vampire?","content":"If Mage had received the book count of Vampire, what additional books would you have want to see written?<br /> <br /> This is partly to ask &quot;what areas does the community wish had more coverage&quot; and also by omission &quot;what areas have enough coverage&quot;. Maybe Storyteller's Vault will grant some wishes. :3<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T13:52:15-08:00","id":1265568,"title":"","content":"This is a game I like to play with a lot of gamelines. I think they would get a lot more lore, and historical accounts. We would finally get actual attention paid to Archmage rules, and we would get sorcerer rules. We would also probably get setting books like think instead of Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom or Kindred of the East books like Ascension War India and the Five Metal Dragons.<br /> <br /> We would get a lot more canon characters cross referenced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T13:52:29-08:00","id":1265569,"title":"","content":"A few things<br /> - I would have liked a &quot;Book of the disparate&quot;, not as in &quot;Guide to the craft&quot;, but a list of possible cabals, little craft, sub traditions,etc... giving potential little groups and potential plot points.<br /> With the sheer possibilities of the setting, there should have been a book made on the groups only mentionned here and there like the sub traditions in the guide to the traditions.<br /> <br /> Not that I don't like the main factions, but the traditions and conventions end up being repetitive and too specific to englob the possible groups that wouls appear in such a world.<br /> <br /> -a &quot;beckett&quot;'s ascension war diary.<br /> <br /> Plot hooks, or the possible use of some left in the older books, what of this sub tradition pretending to speak of an alternate universe where the traditions stand better than this one? What of the attempt of Jules Vernes to create an AI that would be more powerful than the consensus? What of the utopian conspiracy and the possible schism of the conventions?<br /> <br /> -A book of the deep umbra/universe<br /> <br /> The cosmology of mage is big, even though a lot is discussed in other WOD books, but mages are the most interested into the deep umbra, a book for &quot;high leveled&quot; mages, what they could find there, what may happens in a place outside of human consensus, possible alien or frighteningly familiar entities they may find...<br /> <br /> -on the same theme, more groups centered about specific things in the umbra, there is strangely few dream based mage groups or space based non technocrats ones.<br /> <br /> -Most important, a &quot;Book of ascension&quot; based on the long term goals of mages, little and great.<br /> It's funny and all to concentrate on how they awakened, what is their place in chantry/global politics, but one of the themes of mage is the quest for more, even the &quot;master of the art&quot; book is more about power and the daily life of archmasters and less about their end goals.<br /> <br /> For a game based on people fighting for their visions of the perfect world, we're told an awfully few about it.<br /> <br /> And for the tellurian's sake, a real talk about ascension.<br /> <br /> Going all &quot;how could we mortal understand such concept&quot; is a bad excuse, it doesn't make ascension criptic and mysterious. <br /> <br /> Is it too much to ask a storyteller guide to the ascension?<br /> <br /> Not asking definite answer, but potential (and contradictory) possibilities, legends, in short, a guide of how to build the ST vision(s) of ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T14:26:19-08:00","id":1265582,"title":"","content":"A book about Cabals, Amalgams, and Ahrimans ( The Nephandi's equivalent of Cabals ) ; possibly also about groups of Mages from outside the three main Mage factions. Detailing how groups of Mages form, how they function, how they differ from each other, and how they change a Mage's life ; and how they influence the Magick of a Mage.<br /> <br /> A series of three books, each one detailing three of the Spheres / kinds of Magick. My suggestion for the division of the kinds of Magick : Prime, Mind, Spirit / Correspondence, Time, Entropy / Life, Matter, Forces . Or it could be a series of nine books, one for each kind of Magick.<br /> The books would describe the Spells and other related abilities of a given kind of Magick, the consequences of delving into and using it, the differing perspectives about it, specialities and variants, research and tutelage, and approaches and methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-08-2018, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T14:59:31-08:00","id":1265592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1265582#post1265582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three books, each detailing three of the Spheres / kinds of Magick. My suggestion for the division of the kinds of Magick : Prime, Mind, Spirit / Correspondence, Time, Entropy / Life, Matter Forces . Or it could be nine books, one for each kind of Magick. The books would describe the Spells and other related abilities of a given kind of Magick, the consequences of delving into and using it, the differing perspectives about it, specialities and variants, research and tutelage, and approaches and methods.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A billion time yes. Books of sphere would be a great idea, giving advise on the impact of one's sphere on the life of a mage, how he relate to others, and little things that would make the difference between a time master and any other mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T17:11:40-08:00","id":1265623,"title":"","content":"A book on mages houses, because book of havens exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T18:35:47-08:00","id":1265639,"title":"","content":"A few years ago, as a creative exercise, I tried to figure out how I might've developed Mage (and all the other games) from the beginning with the benefits of hindsight and experience. A few of the things I wish Mage had included originally are as follows:<br /> <br /> <b>Witchunters</b> - I would've made this the fourth product in the line, a collection of antagonists and threats for Storytellers to use, divided into four chapters. The Mundane World, including environmental hazards, animals, mortal hindrances such as police, criminals, and the media, as well as unawakened cults, the mentally unbalanced, meddling kids, and the like. Also the Arcanum, Society of Leopold and Twilight Agencies. The Invisible World of spirits, with multiple types - elementals, demons, angels, alien beings, weird conceptual beings, ancient gods, ghosts and fey (this would've predated Wraith and Changeling) - of various power levels. The Awakened, including rivals, rogues/outlaws who've violated Tradition rules, dangerous Orphans, forces of the Technocracy, agents of the Nephandi, and Marauders. And the Supernatural, which at this point would've primarily been vampires and were beasts (without using any nomenclature from the other games), as well as Bygones (both old and new), the Created (homunculi, Frankenstein monsters, sentient robots, etc.), and bizarre urban legends like the Midnight Express ghost train, the 13th Floor, and whatever other stuff writers could come up with. (Every game would've had one of these books - Nightstalkers, Wolfsbane, The Quick &amp; The Dead, Grimm Fears, and Wolves at the Door.)<br /> <br /> <b>Modern Magic</b> - the fifth book, a guide for players and storytellers about being a Mage in the modern World of Darkness, spending a lot of time talking about thing like having to hide your identity from the Technocracy, opting to live off the grid, and gradually losing touch with regular people. Also modern superstitions, religious rituals, and various mystic threads Mages can tap into, the various battle grounds of the Ascension War, and a catalog of modern style Rotes, Bygones, Talismans and other goodies.<br /> <br /> <b>The Crossover Guides</b> - This would've been a series of books for all the lines, all along the same structure. A chapter about how the two groups cross paths, areas of common interest and conflict, factions in each game that deal with the other, and a bunch of premade NPCs; A pair of chapters looking at the signature cities of each line and what the other group is doing there (Mystic Chicago, for example), and a premade crossover chronicle that can be set in either city. Mage's books would've been <i>Blood Magic</i> (Vampire), <i>Savage Magic Mystic Moon</i> (Werewolf), <i>Dead Magic</i> (Wraith) and <i>Mystic Zenith</i> (Changeling).<br /> <br /> <b>Seekers of Ascension</b> - Mage's Who's Who book, with write ups for the game's signature characters, the leaders of the Traditions, important NPCs, chantry leaders and curious characters from around the world, as well as dangerous and infamous members of the Technocracy, Nephandi and other groups.<br /> <br /> <b>Chantry, Sanctum and Cabal </b>- A book about the strongholds of the Awakened, with chapters expanding on the Sanctum background, how Chantries work and are formed, including their various offices, how Mages organize themselves in cities and other geographic areas, and a further look at Cabals, including how and why they form, purposes they have and how they interact with each other. There'd be sample Sanctums, Chantries and Cabals, the last being suitable as allies, rivals or even enemies for the PC cabal.<br /> <br /> <b>The Technomancers' Toolbox</b> - A players guide for technomancers, looking at the history of the art, it's place in the various Traditions (including factions in each sect), a bunch of new Rotes, Talismans, and the like, and some premade character templates (one for each Essence). This would've been the first of a series, with others including <i>Skin-Changers</i> (shapeshifting), <i>Healing Hands</i> (healers, obviously), <i>Hearts &amp; Minds</i> (Ars Cupidae), and <i>Second Sight</i> (seers). The exception to this formula would've been spirit-talkers, who would be covered in ...<br /> <br /> <b>The Spirit Ways</b> - (Yes, I repurposed a lot of older titles) A guide to spirits and the Invisible World for the Awakened. A full catalog of spirit types and their powers, the various spirit courts with their protocols and politics, deals and pacts with spirits, designing your own spirits, and places where they congregate in the material world. Also the players guide to spirit talkers.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizard's March</b> - the Awakened guide to war, including the ritualized combat between members of the Traditions, the shadow wars over influence and lore in the World of Darkness, and the Ascension War against the Technocracy and Nephandi. Also a look at real world military style gear that characters might get their hands on, and premade chronicles.<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Magic</b> - A guide to the morally questionable areas of magic, including necromancy, demonology, blood magic, chaos magic, cursing, and mad science.<br /> <br /> <b>Tales of Magic: Occult Horror/Arcane Mystery/Mystic Romance</b> - a tetralogy of books (the other being <i>Dark Adventure</i>) for Storytellers looking at different genres and how to use them in Mage. Examining the genre, it's variations and subgenres, genre tropes, archetypical NPCs and plots, etc. And premade chronicles.<br /> <br /> <b>Destiny's Price</b> - (Another repurposed title), a look at the high cost of being Awakened, with chapters looking at the toll magic and the Ascension War take on one socially, mentally, physically, and spiritually.<br /> <br /> <b>Scourge: The Book of Paradox </b>- basically everything you would ever want to know about the subject, including it's various manifestations, how and why it happens, Mages who investigate and study it, and more Paradox Spirits than you can shake a broken wand at.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence of Magic: Book of Avatars</b> - A look at the four avatar essences in greater detail and how they function in Mage society (sort of like Werewolf's book of Auspices).<br /> <br /> <b>Cabinet of Curiosities</b> - A collection of oddities and weirdness which often defy the rules as Mage's understand them. Strange relics, mysterious artifacts, lost tomes, cursed objects, and alien items, all with plot hooks and potential chronicle ideas.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 11-09-2018, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T18:45:44-08:00","id":1265641,"title":"","content":"Sphere book , Rote book.<br /> <br /> And , Maybe they can be as powerful as Vampires normally (Yeah , normally , new-born and normal mages are weaker than vampires generally )? The reason why Vampire has so many books is that V:tM is the most popular , and books WW published strengthen Vampire's common Power at last unintentionally (To tell the truth , I always think Vampires are more powerful than other races in most conditions ... )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 12-04-2018, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T23:18:27-08:00","id":1265702,"title":"","content":"<b>Mage: Ascended beings and Gods</b> a book about what ascension is , the archmages and the Exarchs.The supernal exist along imperial magic and the reality is more static than what the consensus could make you think becuase everything is a reflection of the supernal , a mere shadow.Also rules for ascended beings and the avatars being fallen supernal being triying to create archmages to fight back the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage:Unlimited Horizon</b> a book about the mage cosmology , planes and realms full of weirdness and interesting characters.It will include a bestiary of monsters and being from other planes.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage:The Failure:</b>What happens when a mage hubris grow to big? buy this book to discover the greatest botches of all mage history and it\u00b4s consecuences in the world<br /> <br /> <b>Mage:Cabals of the world:</b>A book about mage characters and cabals around the world , their objetives , what are they doing and their relationship in similar line to chicago by night books and Children of the night.<br /> <br /> <b>Fallen Guide to the Nephandi:</b>A guide about the nephadi factions that exist within the traditions and the technocrazy and their way of working.Also better rules for the qlipothic speheres instead of extra paradox you are trapped in a caul for a time acording to the succes of the paradox roll.Also a talk a about being that almost descended ceasin to exist the Qli eldricht abovinations from previous universes that rage against the world for they being trapped forever in a caul until they manage to attain a soul basically they are what the baali make deals and fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 11-09-2018, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T04:46:29-08:00","id":1265761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1265702#post1265702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mage: Ascended beings and Gods</b> a book about what ascension is , the archmages and the Exarchs.The supernal exist along imperial magic and the reality is more static than what the consensus could make you think becuase everything is a reflection of the supernal , a mere shadow.Also rules for ascended beings and the avatars being fallen supernal being triying to create archmages to fight back the Exarchs.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Awakening mytho don't mix well with Ascension cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T05:30:53-08:00","id":1265771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1265641#post1265641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Rote book (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that a book in regard to Conjunctional Magick would be very interesting ; I also think it is needed to further define and improve M:tA.<br /> It could discuss many issues. Which kinds of Magick serve as the basis, and which are the addition in a Conjunctional Effect ; can this distinction always be made in regard to a Conjunctional Effect ? Which parts of a Conjunctional Effect can be done with other kinds of Magick interchangeably ? Are Effects which include just one kind of Magick sometimes more potent, and are Mages who do so as a rule more capable in some ways ? How does Conjunctional Magick differ from Mage to Mage, and from Paradigm to Paradigm ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1265623#post1265623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A book on mages houses, because book of havens exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is the Book of Chantries. But I understand that this is probably not what you mean.<br /> I think that Sanctums, and other special places related to Mages or places that Mages use, should definitely be detailed in a separate book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T06:02:36-08:00","id":1265781,"title":"","content":"A Revised Player's Guide (that should include a good section about Rotes), because the Book of Shadows it's painfully old<br /> <br /> A Revised Book of Chantries would be good too, as stuff changed and many chantries were destroyed.<br /> <br /> A book on the same vein as Spirit Ways, but about the occidental Traditions: True Names, High Ritual Hermetiscism/Gnosticism, Verbena Druidism, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T07:26:54-08:00","id":1265816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1265781#post1265781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A book on the same vein as Spirit Ways, but about the occidental Traditions: True Names, High Ritual Hermetiscism/Gnosticism, Verbena Druidism, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to see one on weird/Obsolete scientific theories for the SOE, or on actual wild scientific implication for the VA and technocracy<br /> <br /> In truth, I think Mage require a Book of science, both to present science as it works in real life and the implication of the game's cosmology on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T09:05:57-08:00","id":1265839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1265761#post1265761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awakening mytho don't mix well with Ascension cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends how do you decide to do that<br /> <br /> If you use a system of tiers a la CoD it will work and the core game won\u00b4t be affected at all","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T09:59:14-08:00","id":1265855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1265569#post1265569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Most important, a &quot;Book of ascension&quot; based on the long term goals of mages, little and great.<br /> It's funny and all to concentrate on how they awakened, what is their place in chantry/global politics, but one of the themes of mage is the quest for more, even the &quot;master of the art&quot; book is more about power and the daily life of archmasters and less about their end goals.<br /> <br /> For a game based on people fighting for their visions of the perfect world, we're told an awfully few about it.<br /> <br /> And for the tellurian's sake, a real talk about ascension.<br /> <br /> Going all &quot;how could we mortal understand such concept&quot; is a bad excuse, it doesn't make ascension criptic and mysterious.<br /> <br /> Is it too much to ask a storyteller guide to the ascension?<br /> <br /> Not asking definite answer, but potential (and contradictory) possibilities, legends, in short, a guide of how to build the ST vision(s) of ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>As it is, Ascension is far more vague and mysterious than Golconda in Vampire ... ironic, as Mage was supposed to be more hopeful than Vampire in that <i>every </i>mage would be seeking Ascension.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T14:21:28-08:00","id":1265922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1265816#post1265816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see one on weird/Obsolete scientific theories for the SOE, or on actual wild scientific implication for the VA and technocracy</div> </div> </div> </div>My Technomancers' Toolbox would've included that. An overview of the basic branches of science, &quot;dead&quot; sciences (alchemy, phrenology, eugenics, etc.), various fringe theories (cold fusion, perpetual motion machines), and some of the weird cutting edge stuff (zero point energy, quantum computing), and how the various Traditions might use them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1265781#post1265781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Revised Book of Chantries would be good too, as stuff changed and many chantries were destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather wish that Mage (along with Werewolf, Wraith and Changeling) had lead with a book about chantries in general - how they work, how to design them, how PCs can found their own, how to use them in your games, etc. - and later on done a Book of Chantries that detailed 9 or 10 interesting locations around the globe.<br /> <br /> As for a Players Guide, I think my ideal one would've been:<ul><li>An in depth look at the physiology, psychology and metaphysics of the Awakened. How they think, how their bodies work, the impact of Avatar and Essence on personality, questions of lifespan, insanity (without becoming a Marauder), reincarnation, reproduction, and all those assorted niggling questions players tend to have.</li> <li>An expanded look at the various traits - Attributes, Abilities, Backgrounds and the rest - with alternate creation rules, new uses for skills, what it means to have a Trait above normal human limits, different ways backgrounds can manifest, and merits/flaws.</li> <li>An expanded look at each of the Traditions (and the Hollow Ones), including basic history, philosophies, their leadership, primary chantry, and a premade character template for each.</li> <li>A chapter on how individual Mages fit into the Awakened society, starting with their Cabal, and moving up through the levels of Chantry, city/geographic area, Tradition, and the Nine Mystical Traditions as a whole.</li> <li>More about magic, starting with each Sphere and what going above Master level might mean for each, and a bunch of new Rotes and Talismans.</li> <li>The initial group write ups for the main Crafts (I probably would restrict this to eight of them, otherwise it would be far too big).</li> <li>An appendix about creating unAwakened characters (acolytes and others), including three or four basic sorcery Paths.</li> </ul>Or something similar to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 11-09-2018, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T14:33:39-08:00","id":1265925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1265922#post1265922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My Technomancers' Toolbox would've included that. An overview of the basic branches of science, &quot;dead&quot; sciences (alchemy, phrenology, eugenics, etc.), various fringe theories (cold fusion, perpetual motion machines), and some of the weird cutting edge stuff (zero point energy, quantum computing), and how the various Traditions might use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technomancers' Toybox is kinda out of date as it is - some of those Devices are downright sleepertech at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 11-09-2018, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T14:57:46-08:00","id":1265935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1265925#post1265925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technomancers' Toolbox is kinda out of date as it is - some of those Devices are downright sleepertech at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may be thinking of the Technomancers' <b>Toy</b>box, which is not the same as the proposed theoretical sourcebook I mentioned in my first post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T16:05:29-08:00","id":1265961,"title":"","content":"I'd like a series of smaller books \u2014 averaging, say, 32 pages or less \u2014 dedicated to M20's Foci (I'm sorry; but sometimes you just can't get away from the plural of the word). Each one would be centered on one Practice. <br /> <br /> It would start with a chapter on Theory, which would discuss the three or four most relevant Paradigms in terms of how they relate to the book's Practice; then a chapter on the Practice itself, which would discuss the Abilities, Instruments, and Spheres as they relate to the Practice along with a selection of Rotes that don't just specify what Spheres you need and what effect you achieve, but also what Instruments you might use and how you'd use them, and what Abilities could be used to enhance the effect. It would also discuss how the mystic/technomancer divide applies to the Practice: some Practices heavily favor a technomantic mindset, others favor a more mystical Monday, and still others see frequency use by both.<br /> <br /> It would then wrap up with a selection of Wonders that someone of that Practice would find useful \u2014 or, in the case of Practices that are heavily into making Wonders, the sorts of things a practitioner might make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T10:39:40-08:00","id":1266230,"title":"","content":"I think that a section ( or multiple sections ) in a book should discuss and define more the distinctions and qualities of different Foci ; for example there are Foci which are items, and there are Foci which are actions or maintaining a lifestyle.<br /> Benefits and limitations of different Foci should be brought up and explored - for example Foci which are hard to carry, are very fragile, or require some set-up time. The opposites of these qualities ( easy to carry, durable etc. ) should be considered and discussed, as well.<br /> Also, the idea and concept of Foci being tied to specific kinds of Magick ( and maybe to specific Effects ) should definitely be explored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-10-2018, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T08:42:33-08:00","id":1266420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1265623#post1265623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A book on mages houses, because book of havens exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. Book of Chantries? It is a thing you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T21:13:48-08:00","id":1266605,"title":"","content":"You know what I'd like to have seen more of? Adventure modules.<br /> <br /> Mage has always been very light on pre-packaged adventures or stories. Lots of material that suggest plot hooks the Storytellers could implement, but few complete stories.<br /> <br /> The reason why is obvious, of course. By nature of their expansive powers, Mages can do theoretically anything. Which makes it difficult to plan a story around, at least in the manner that White Wolf's writers were always accustomed to. Just look at how rail-roady the Vampire modules had to get to accomplish their narrative ends. And Vampires have finite supernatural abilities at their disposal. I suspect White Wolf looked at the Spheres and gave up on ever formulating adventures the players couldn't easily - trivially - bypass.<br /> <br /> My argument is that this stems from a failure in the writing process. Or, rather, a too strict adherence to traditional writing. (See the aforementioned Vampire railroading). If you're going to create modules for Mage, you need to have less &quot;Plots to Follow&quot;, and more &quot;Problems to Solve&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mage, being an open-ended experience, needs more open-ended conflicts. Villains that aren't shackled to individual schemes, but engage in schemes to pursue their more general goals. Conflicts that don't rely on the game hitting the exact story beats, but where the &quot;plot&quot; organically arises from the NPCs pursuing goals and the players acting in response to them. Preferably, the conflict is like a multi-headed beast; even if the cabal solves one problem, it doesn't invalidate the menace of multiple others. And if you had a module like this, they would need to explain the motivations and personalities of the principle NPCs, such that a Storyteller always knows how they would react to a given situation.<br /> <br /> And, of course, the modules would need to take into account all nine Spheres, and how the presence or absence of them can further the narrative towards some conclusion. Everyone always complains about murder mysteries being impossible to run, because &quot;anyone with Time 2 can solve it instantly&quot;. Those who put a little effort in will know that it doesn't have to be that simple, and a Mage module would need to put just as much care into filling those holes. Even if it's as simple as &quot;there was a Time ward blocking post-cognition&quot;, or &quot;the killer was wearing a mask&quot;, or &quot;you see the killer...and you have no idea who this is&quot;.<br /> <br /> In any RPG where players can specialize in their characters's capabilities, you need to leave multiple ways to arrive at the answers. Pre-packaged adventures aren't impossible in Mage. They just require a radically different design philosophy, in comparison to a linear succession of areas and story beats that follow a single plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T08:53:46-08:00","id":1266713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1266605#post1266605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My argument is that this stems from a failure in the writing process. Or, rather, a too strict adherence to traditional writing. (See the aforementioned Vampire railroading). If you're going to create modules for Mage, you need to have less &quot;Plots to Follow&quot;, and more &quot;Problems to Solve&quot;.<br /> (...)<br /> And, of course, the modules would need to take into account all nine Spheres, and how the presence or absence of them can further the narrative towards some conclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>If adventure modules would be done under the assumption that Magick can easily solve obstacles and problems - which I think is true to a much lesser extent than it might first seem to be - then the challenge could come in the vein of &quot; How the objectives are accomplished. &quot; rather than &quot; Will the objectives be accomplished ? &quot; .<br /> <br /> There are other factors to consider as well : avoiding the Domino Effect ( Coincidental Spells become harder to cast if the same circumstances are used again and again ) , Paradox, mundane humans finding out anything ( not just about the use of Magick or the existence of Mages, but also the involvement of the PCs, and anything unusual happening ) , and other Mages who shouldn't know finding out what is happening. Also, the PCs might have limitations - or opt to take some upon them - because of their Paradigm, dealings with other Mages, or researching a particular use of Magick. An approach could be assumed in regard to use of Magick : how can a Mage become skilled in particular kind of Effect if they use it on every occasion, out of convenience ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1266605#post1266605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone always complains about murder mysteries being impossible to run, because &quot;anyone with Time 2 can solve it instantly&quot;. Those who put a little effort in will know that it doesn't have to be that simple, and a Mage module would need to put just as much care into filling those holes. Even if it's as simple as &quot;there was a Time ward blocking post-cognition&quot;, or &quot;the killer was wearing a mask&quot;, or &quot;you see the killer...and you have no idea who this is&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think by default the description of Time 2 suffices in regard to Time 2 not solving every mystery easily : &quot; (...) those impressions are fleeting, hazy, not entirely accurate, and bound by the limitations of that time and place ( that is, what a bystander in that specific time and location could sense under the circumstances ) (...) &quot; .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1266605#post1266605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any RPG where players can specialize in their characters's capabilities, you need to leave multiple ways to arrive at the answers. Pre-packaged adventures aren't impossible in Mage. They just require a radically different design philosophy, in comparison to a linear succession of areas and story beats that follow a single plot.</div> </div> </div> </div>One option is to introduce a highly skilled rival or enemy Mage in an adventure. Relying too much on the use of Magick will turn the adventure - as if the PCs might have wished for it - into one entirely about Magick and Spells ; as the NPC Mage(s) start hiding and clouding the use of Magick in the area, disrupting and falsifying the PCs' use of Magick, and tracking and investigating the PCs through the Effects that they use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T16:53:20-08:00","id":1266818,"title":"","content":"I think the book count for Mage was actually pretty high, in the heyday at least, and wouldm't have been far off Vampire. Anyway, the thing that Mage really missed in my view was more scenario and campaign books. Something like Chicago by Night or some road-trip adventure would have made the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T19:14:19-08:00","id":1266838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1266420#post1266420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh. Book of Chantries? It is a thing you know.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is different than &quot;Book of random vampire's houses&quot; chantries are on par with a city setting at the least. Plus it has how to built it.. really its closer to Damnation City from Requiem than Book of Havens..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T18:34:41-08:00","id":1268114,"title":"","content":"(I figured I'd throw this out there. Someone may want to take part of it and develop it for the ST Vault or something.)<br /> <br /> Chantry Sanctum and Cabal - A book of gatherings and strongholds for Mage: The Ascension<br /> <br /> Chapter One: Sanctums<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">An in-depth revisitation and expansion of the Sanctum background, including optional rules for Sanctum creation by use of building points and features (such as tools, security systems and the like). Selecting a location, how to prepare and equip the site, and mystical attuning oneself to the Sanctum. The idea of naturally occurring Sanctums and how they fit different Traditions. Mages sharing Sanctums and how that works, as well as what happens when a Mage takes over and claims a preexisting Sanctum. The specific needs and specifications for each of the Traditions and for the more common styles of magic (enchanting/craftwork, religious ritual, spirit-talking, etc.), and ways to do personal customization. And the idea of Sanctum resonance and having an affinity for a certain Sphere. <br /> And a collection of sample Sanctums: The Craftsman's Workshop, The Family Crypt, The High Tech Lab, The Meditative Garden, The Occult Mystic Circle, The Primitive Shaman Lodge, and The Private Alter. </div> Chapter Two: Cabals<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">How and why Cabals form. The common types of Cabals - Single Tradition, Cultural (those who all share similar backgrounds and/or mystical styles), Research/Discovery, Combat (especially in the Ascension War), and Political. Roles within the Cabal, including The Face, The Fixer, The Muscle, The Pointman, The Pillar, The Leader, and The Devil's Advocate (members may take one multiple or none of these roles). Rules/guidelines for pooling character background points for the Cabal, including for group Mentors or Followers. And understanding the Cabal's place in the greater Awakened world, such as relations with other Cabals, with various Chantries, and role in the Ascension War. <br /> Then three sample Cabals to serve as possible allies, rivals or enemies of the player characters' Cabal. <br /> <i>The Voodoo History Society</i> - a research Cabal devoted to unearthing secret history, exposing conspiracies and recovering lost wonders. Led by Dr. Patricia Talib, Hermetic linguistics prodigy of House Bonisagus; with Stewart Little (Virtual Adept historian and journalist), Raveka (Dreamspeaker Baruti ghost-chaiser and storyteller), and John Goodson (Euthanatos homicide detective and truth seeker). <br /> <i>The Lunatic Express</i> - a war Cabal who perform random and often violent attacks against what they perceive to be Technocratic interests. Led by Lucian Shepherd, Akashic radical anti-materialist anarchist of the LiHai; with Diamond Dog (last of the die-hard Virtual Adapt cyberpunk warriors), Hashim (radical Ecstatic gnostic terrorist fanatic), and Mary Ninekills (Dreamspeakers AWOL US Marine of the Red Spears. <br /> <i>\u200bThe Diamond Heart Gang</i> - a political Cabal focused on accumulating financial power in as flashy a manor as possible. Led by Diana Chaucer, Verbena financial witch; with Kim Ben-Hwa (former Korean boy band idol now face and negotiator for the Akashic She Ren), Professor Bruce Botwell (Etheric utopian political theorist and stock market mavin), and Jenifer Lebeau (financial prodigy and member of a Celestial Chorus sacred messianic bloodline). </div> Chapter Three: Chantries<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The role of Chantries in Awakened Society and their place in the Ascension War. How Chantries are founded and created, including those planned and designed vs those that spontaneously or accidentally come about. How Chantries grow and evolve, their defense and security, and the recruiting of new members. Leadership and management of Chantries, the positions of responsibility (similar to some of the ones you'd see in Werewolf Caerns), and diplomacy with outsiders. The Logistic of Chantry management, including staffing, housing and utilities, mystical resources, and keeping away unwanted attention. Fitting personal Sanctums into a Chantry, and other unique features and abilities a Chantry might have (stable gateways into the Umbra, wellsprings of Quintessence, etc.)<br /> Several sample Chantries (or at least the broad outlines of them) that can be dropped into most city settings without much trouble. <br /> <i>The Fort Building</i> - an old building originally built along mystical parameters (similar to Ghostbusters), renovated into loft apartments that now house a variety of Bohemian artists and eccentric oddballs, several of whom serve as Acolytes and other allies (and as potential Changeling crossover hooks if you want to go that way), with the Chantry proper taking up an entire floor to itself as well as a number of hidden rooms scattered throughout the building. <br /> <i>Fox Glove Farms</i> - A small family owned organic farm that also plays host to an artists colony, a Wiccan coven and/or a children's day camp. <br /> <i>The Greymalkin Detective Agency</i> - a long established private investigation firm which specializes in cases of an unusual nature, often employing individuals with strange abilities (including the Mage Cabals which make up the Chantry).<br /> <i>The Time Warp </i><i>Theater </i>- a renovated Art Deco theater building specializing in showing classic films and doing live stage shows (usually plays or performance art but sometime music), time and space sometimes play by different rules here, with patrons (PCs or otherwise) finding themselves going back to critical points in their lives or in history, like an episode of the Twilight Zone. <br /> <i>Turnkey Labs</i> - a private technological think tank and engineering research lab that specializes in pushing the limits of what people think technology can do, mainly because they do a lot of work in technomancy. Their overall philosophy is one of technology as a means of wonder and liberation rather than control and conformity. <br /> Also a brief description of the central Chantry for each of the Traditions (The Akashic Record, etc.)</div> Chapter Four: Councils <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The local leadership of a geographic area (say, Seattle), usually including several local earthbound Chantries, with members representing said Chantries or Cabals (or sometimes Traditions or other local power blocs). The various rules and protocols said Councils establish, various positions (Heralds, for example). Issues of etiquette, diplomacy, justice and punishment. Official council gatherings and Tribunals. PCs as members of the Council and taking roles of leadership in the region and the Tradition. </div> Appendix: Wellsprings (ie, sources of Quintessence)<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The hows and whys of Quintessence flowing into the material world, the impact any Resonance from the flow might have on the location and nearby people, conflicts over them that might arise with other supernatural beings. <br /> Sample wellsprings, including the Hidden Glade, the Ancient Ruin, the Physics Collider, the Playground and the Mausoleum. <br /> A look at some legendary sites such as Stonehenge, Ayers Rock, Mt. Fuji, the Nazca Lines, the Tunguska blast site, and the Trinity test site. </div> <br /> <br /> And then an alternate Book of Chantries that would've detailed 9 or 10 interesting places around the world, probably half of them single Tradition ones and the other half mixed. Not sure exactly what it would include, other than the Coyote Caravan, a traveling Chantry of the Cult of Ecstasy's 5th World Tribe, a collection of hippies, Bohemians and other oddballs which roams the American Southwest spreading their beliefs of a more natural and spiritually oriented lifestyle of music, handcrafts, and vision quests. That and probably Grimm's Occult Specialty Shoppe, which would use Correspondence magic to colocate in multiple cities at the same time. Other thoughts that had occurred to me were an Akashic capoeira school/candomble temple in Sao Luis and a Jerbiton Hermetic piazza in Milan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T12:30:30-08:00","id":1268364,"title":"","content":"Another possibility for a book is making one that concerns systems of interactions between Mages ( and other supernaturals, if they involve themselves ) in regard to particular interests. The areas of interests that come to my mind are trading magical items and magical lore ( whether in established locations or just through arranged meetings ) , Quintessence-related knowledge and activities, Umbra and Spirits related activities and knowledge, and information trading and brokering. These areas of interests should have their own separate communities, societies, and organizations formed around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T13:08:40-08:00","id":1268379,"title":"","content":"An Osirean league book, covering the origins of the web of Faith and all the Mummy Stuff but with an emphasis on the Mages and Sorcerers and how they Pioneered the Heku rituals and Powers. With info on the Cult of Isis, Children of Osiris who became human and cultivated magic, and the Mortal Mages of the Followers of Set. Big info on the multiple Spells of Life and it\u2019s evolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T13:25:13-08:00","id":1268390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1268379#post1268379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Osirean league book, covering the origins of the web of Faith and all the Mummy Stuff but with an emphasis on the Mages and Sorcerers and how they Pioneered the Heku rituals and Powers. With info on the Cult of Isis, Children of Osiris who became human and cultivated magic, and the Mortal Mages of the Followers of Set. Big info on the multiple Spells of Life and it\u2019s evolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could be part of a book that would detail Mages cooperating with Vampires, Garou, Changelings, Wraiths, and possibly other supernaturals. Magick Effect are very useful in supporting other persons. This book would detail how cooperating with other supernaturals than Mages can change a Mage's Paradigm, Magick, and outlook.<br /> Did you read anything about Mages of the Followers of Set in any book ; or do you just assume that it is a possibility ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T13:44:58-08:00","id":1268396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1268390#post1268390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This could be part of a book that would detail Mages cooperating with Vampires, Garou, Changelings, Wraiths, and possibly other supernaturals. Magick Effect are very useful in supporting other persons. This book would detail how cooperating with other supernaturals than Mages can change a Mage's Paradigm, Magick, and outlook.<br /> Did you read anything about Mages of the Followers of Set in any book ; or do you just assume that it is a possibility ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just my headcanon, since they have 4 Jar Demon slaves and mortal cultists are supposed to be spiritually shepherded as well. Figured they didn\u2019t always just use vampire Lector Priests. But even other clans were accepted as faithful so why not grow your own Mages and Sorcerers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T18:17:11-08:00","id":1268447,"title":"","content":"A book about the war between Horus and Set would probably be a World of Darkness book, talking about the ancient Setites, who/what Osiris might've been (probably with 3 or 4 possibilities that Storytellers could tailer to fit their needs), the ancient shapeshifters of Egypt (including the pre-curse Silent Striders, the Mokole of the Nile, the Bubasti back in their zenith, and what other breeds like the Ananasi or Nagah would've been doing at the time), the concept of Apep as a avatar of the Wyrm, all of the mystical sects devoted to the various Egyptian gods (Isis, Osiris, Thoth, Ptah, Sebek, Ra, etc.), the original Mummies and what they were like back then before having centuries of experience under their belts, the Egyptian underworld of the time (including Anubis and the first Ferrymen), various Egyptian bygones, the djinn and other spirits/fey. Such a book has the potential to be pretty cool. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T03:25:21-08:00","id":1268505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1268396#post1268396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just my headcanon, since they have 4 Jar Demon slaves and mortal cultists are supposed to be spiritually shepherded as well. Figured they didn\u2019t always just use vampire Lector Priests. But even other clans were accepted as faithful so why not grow your own Mages and Sorcerers!</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense, but it also does lead to a question : why hasn't pretty much everyone else done this ? ( Well, the Tal'Mahe'Ra Vampires do it. ) While this leads to the notion that it is not as easy, and the possibility not as apparent, as it might seem. What characteristics would Followers of Set have as a group that would make them capable of either recruiting Mages or creating circumstances for persons Awakening ? Mages are rare and they tend to be contacted and recruited by other Mages after Awakening. Leading a person to an Awakening is something that requires exceptional skills and very noteworthy persons.<br /> Though it could be said that it used to be different in the ancient times, with Mages living more openly and also being willing to consider more possibilities than keeping to themselves. Also, it is likely that during the times before the Traditions, the Order of Reason ( and later the Technocracy ) , and the Nephandi were formed as factions, Mages were much less likely to be recruited into a Mage-focused group as quickly as it occurs in the modern era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-18-2018, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T10:54:57-08:00","id":1268581,"title":"","content":"Ghouls with low levels of (I'm blanking on the current term for Setite blood magic), maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T11:06:26-08:00","id":1268582,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m saying Followers of Set specifically because they have an established Paradigm and system of Foci. And are supposed to cultivate spirituality in their cult. Mages would be rare for them but I believe Sorcerers would be a bit more common as they can be trained from the ground up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T11:42:05-08:00","id":1268597,"title":"","content":"Yeah, their own version/counterpart of the Children of Osiris or Cult of Isis sect would be perfectly doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T10:09:12-08:00","id":1269275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1266818#post1266818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the book count for Mage was actually pretty high, in the heyday at least, and wouldm't have been far off Vampire. Anyway, the thing that Mage really missed in my view was more scenario and campaign books. Something like Chicago by Night or some road-trip adventure would have made the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I count 73 books published for mage that were not fiction, combinations of other books, or associated materials (screens, tarot deck) and 120 for Vampire: The Masquerade. I may have missed a few for Vampire. I'm not counting Dark Ages, Sorcerer's Crusade, etc either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T13:33:44-08:00","id":1269332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1269275#post1269275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) I'm not counting Dark Ages, Sorcerer's Crusade, etc either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are you not counting those books ? I think that the Dark Ages books are wholly part of their respective games ; and they are also fully part of World of Darkness as a setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T07:34:24-08:00","id":1269558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1269332#post1269332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why are you not counting those books ? I think that the Dark Ages books are wholly part of their respective games ; and they are also fully part of World of Darkness as a setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't include them as they get their own core rule book. If I did, vampire had some 30 Dark Ages books, another 4 Victorian ones, where mage had 10 sorcerer's crusade books and 2 dark ages books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T06:14:52-08:00","id":1270334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1268582#post1268582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m saying Followers of Set specifically because they have an established Paradigm and system of Foci. And are supposed to cultivate spirituality in their cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the Followers of Set having beliefs that could be the basis of a Mage's Paradigm do you mean the &quot;Down with the Aeons&quot; outlook and approach ; or something else ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T12:21:18-08:00","id":1270398,"title":"","content":"I mean their Egyptian Gods themed spirituality that is the basis of their Blood Sorcery Akhu. It works in a Dark Age Mage sort of way. They believe in Sutekh as a savior but in general believe they can call upon all the Egyptian deities if proper rituals are observed and they believe the magic is powered by the desecration of ritually prepared dead as they draw power from denying souls the peace Osiris promised. So basically use the write up for Akhu in Blood Sacrifices. It\u2019s good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T21:04:12-08:00","id":1270517,"title":"","content":"Oh and in Lore of the Clans, the Setite section mentions rumors about other supernaturals also being a part of the Faith, so I\u2019ve been doing it as head canon revised but it\u2019s not all just my headcanon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T11:04:27-08:00","id":1270639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1270517#post1270517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh and in Lore of the Clans, the Setite section mentions rumors about other supernaturals also being a part of the Faith, so I\u2019ve been doing it as head canon revised but it\u2019s not all just my headcanon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that there definitely should be some radical and extremist Mages of the Cult of Ecstasy, and former Mages of the CoE, who would be cooperating and spending time with the Followers of Set. The second CoE Tradition Book often mentions how it is a question and an issue as to how far should a member of the Cult of Ecstasy go in trying to show the myriad possibilities of experiences and the ecstasy to mundane humans. The Followers of Set would probably offer a clear answer and perspective of &quot;As far as you can go, and then some more.&quot; . I can see some Ecstatics being very interested in such an attitude and approach, under the right circumstances. Especially those that are critricized or ostracized by other CoE Mages because of their outlook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-25-2018, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T14:49:13-08:00","id":1270693,"title":"","content":"There's a pretty radical sect of Gnostic extremists from the Ecstatics in the history chapter of Guide to the Traditions (I'm blanking on their name ATM), whose beliefs are fairly compatible with some of the revised Setite ones. Also some of their Discordian and Chaos magician sects. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 11-25-2018, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T11:31:14-08:00","id":1270889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1270639#post1270639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that there definitely should be some radical and extremist Mages of the Cult of Ecstasy, and former Mages of the CoE, who would be cooperating and spending time with the Followers of Set. The second CoE Tradition Book often mentions how it is a question and an issue as to how far should a member of the Cult of Ecstasy go in trying to show the myriad possibilities of experiences and the ecstasy to mundane humans. The Followers of Set would probably offer a clear answer and perspective of &quot;As far as you can go, and then some more.&quot; . I can see some Ecstatics being very interested in such an attitude and approach, under the right circumstances. Especially those that are critricized or ostracized by other CoE Mages because of their outlook.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I imagine its more local than anything else.. there are CoE who might join a settite temple.. or vice versa. But also some hermetics who are &quot;DOING HEKU&quot; and don't want to see people corrupting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T15:04:36-08:00","id":1270940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1270693#post1270693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a pretty radical sect of Gnostic extremists from the Ecstatics in the history chapter of Guide to the Traditions (I'm blanking on their name ATM), whose beliefs are fairly compatible with some of the revised Setite ones. Also some of their Discordian and Chaos magician sects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the Mages of the Hagalaz and the Followers of Set interacting could be very interesting.<br /> The Gnostic extremists Ecstatics - do you mean the Studiosi, the Zelous Ones ; or some other group ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-26-2018, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T15:12:01-08:00","id":1270944,"title":"","content":"The would be them, yes. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T13:18:54-08:00","id":1272681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265523-what-if-mage-has-as-many-books-as-vampire?p=1270889#post1270889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I imagine its more local than anything else.. there are CoE who might join a settite temple.. or vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't have joining a Setite temple in mind in regard to how it would turn out most of the time for the Cultist of Ecstasy. Joining the temple seems hardcore - just think what would happen to the CoE's Kamamarga - she or he would have to build it anew, or abandon it. I mostly had in mind a CoE Mage meeting up with a Follower of Set and just hanging out together, doing regular stuff. Like the Mage taking a lot of drugs, and then letting the Setite drink her or his blood afterwards ; and then drinking the Setite's Vitae and being made a Ghoul. And talking about philosophy, different perspectives and approaches, and what each of them has done lately, and is planning to do in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-03-2018, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T21:09:46-08:00","id":1272769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-clas